  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AECF-Conflict countries - AECF Post Conflict</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AECF-Konfliktl&#xe4;nder</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till entrepren&#xf6;rer i postkonflikt l&#xe4;nder genom Africa Enterprise Challenge Fund. L&#xe4;nder som tillh&#xf6;r m&#xe5;lgruppen &#xe4;r  Liberia, Somalia, DRC,  Sierra Leone och Zimbabwe genom ett seperat f&#xf6;nster.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to a conflict window of the African Agribusiness Enterprise   Challenge Fund. Countries targeted are Liberia, Somalia, DRC, Sierra Leone and Zimbabwe which is handled through a spereate window.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Post Conflict Window (PCW) is a special funding window for inclusive business in agribusiness, agribusiness value chains, and rural financial services in conflict-affected countries. The objective of the intervention is to develop agribusiness and rural finance market systems to benefit the lives of poor rural households across Africa. PCW provides investment support to companies in order to enable them to carry out new and innovative initiatives within the fields of agriculture, rural financing, renewable energy and adaptation to climate change for smallholders in rural Africa. This contribution, the PCW, was designed to provide a positive contribution to pro-poor growth in Sub-Saharan Africa by encouraging private sector investments specifically in the agriculture sectors of African countries emerging from conflict, such as Somalia, Democratic Republic of Congo, Liberia and Sierra Leone.</narrative>
  </description>
